如果设置了每分钟执行一次的 `setInterval` 函数并且执行的代码较长，可能会导致页面卡死。这是因为 `setInterval` 会每分钟触发一次代码执行，如果代码执行时间超过一分钟，那么新的 `setInterval` 触发会在上一个代码执行完成之后立即执行，这样会导致代码一直在运行而无法响应其他的页面事件。

解决这个问题的一种方式是确保代码执行时间不会超过一分钟。你可以检查代码是否存在循环或递归，以及是否有重复的计算或操作。如果有大量的计算或操作，你可以考虑将其拆分成更小的任务，并使用 `setTimeout` 函数来逐步执行。

另一种解决方法是在 `setInterval` 的回调函数中添加一个标志位，以便在代码正在执行时禁止再次触发回调函数。例如：

```
let isRunning = false;

function myFunction() {
  if (isRunning) {
    return;
  }

  isRunning = true;

  // 长时间运行的代码

  isRunning = false;
}

setInterval(myFunction, 60000);
```

这样一来，在代码执行期间，`isRunning` 会被置为 `true`，防止触发新的代码执行。当代码执行完成后，`isRunning` 会被复位为 `false`，这样就可以再次触发 `myFunction`。

总的来说，页面卡死问题可能是由于 `setInterval` 中的代码执行时间过长所导致的。你可以通过优化代码或使用标志位来解决这个问题。

Creating a WordPress plugin that compresses images requires some coding knowledge in PHP, JavaScript, and CSS. In this example, we will create a simple plugin that uses the free open-source image optimization library called reSmush.it to optimize and compress images in WordPress.

1. Start by creating a new folder in your WordPress "wp-content/plugins" directory. Name it "image-compression-plugin" or any name you prefer.

2. Inside this folder, create a new file named "image-compression-plugin.php" and open it in a text editor.

3. Add the following PHP code at the top of the file to define your plugin's basic information:

```php
<?php
/*
Plugin Name: Image Compression Plugin
Plugin URI: https://github.com/my-plugin/image-compression-plugin
Description: Optimizes and compresses images using the reSmush.it API.
Version: 1.0
Author: Your Name
Author URI: https://www.yourwebsite.com
License: GPL2
*/
```

4. Add the "register_activation_hook" and "register_deactivation_hook" functions to enable and disable the plugin:

```php
register_activation_hook( __FILE__, 'image_compression_plugin_activate' );
register_deactivation_hook( __FILE__, 'image_compression_plugin_deactivate' );

function image_compression_plugin_activate() {
    // Activation action
}

function image_compression_plugin_deactivate() {
    // Deactivation action
}
```

5. Include the required filters and actions to hook into WordPress media upload process:

```php
add_filter( 'wp_handle_upload_prefilter', 'image_compression_plugin_prefilter' );
add_filter( 'wp_handle_upload', 'image_compression_plugin_handle_upload' );

function image_compression_plugin_prefilter( $file ) {
    // Check if the file is an image
    if ( substr( $file['type'], 0, 5 ) !== 'image' ) {
        return $file;
    }

    // Set a flag to process the image after uploading
    global $image_compression_plugin_image;
    $image_compression_plugin_image = true;

    return $file;
}

function image_compression_plugin_handle_upload( $fileinfo ) {
    // Check if we should process the image
    global $image_compression_plugin_image;
    if ( !$image_compression_plugin_image ) {
        return $fileinfo;
    }

    // API settings
    $api_url = "http://api.resmush.it/";

    // Check if the uploaded file is an image
    if ( substr( $fileinfo['type'], 0, 5 ) !== 'image' ) {
        return $fileinfo;
    }

    // Build request
    $data = array(
        'files' => new CURLFile( $fileinfo['file'] )
    );

    // Initialize cURL
    $ch = curl_init();
    curl_setopt( $ch, CURLOPT_URL, $api_url );
    curl_setopt( $ch, CURLOPT_POST, 1 );
    curl_setopt( $ch, CURLOPT_RETURNTRANSFER, 1 );
    curl_setopt( $ch, CURLOPT_POSTFIELDS, $data );

    // Call reSmush.it API
    $response = json_decode( curl_exec( $ch ) );
    curl_close( $ch );

    // Check the API response
    if ( isset( $response->dest ) && $response->dest ) {
        // Save the optimized image
        $optimized_image = file_get_contents( $response->dest );
        file_put_contents( $fileinfo['file'], $optimized_image );

        // Update the file size
        $fileinfo['size'] = $response->src_size;
    }

    return $fileinfo;
}
```

6. Save the "image-compression-plugin.php" file and upload the entire "image-compression-plugin" folder to the "wp-content/plugins" directory of your WordPress website.

7. Log in to your WordPress admin panel, go to "Plugins," find your new "Image Compression Plugin," and click "Activate."

Now the plugin will automatically compress uploaded images during the media upload process using the reSmush.it API. Customize the API URL, supported formats, and options to enhance the functionality of the plugin as required.

